* DC motor and L298N dual H-bridge (kisimavr), behavioural models
* kisimavr - SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* MOTOR_DC: small brushed DC motor (6..12 V, about 8500 rpm at 9 V, no load)
* Pins: P N SPEED   (SPEED: voltage output, 1 V = 1000 rpm)
* Electrical: R, L and back-EMF KE * w; mechanical: J dw/dt = KT * i - B * w - TL
* (w in rad/s); mechanical time constant J * R / (KE * KT) = 20 ms.
*   KiCad: Sim.Params = R=2 L=1m KE=0.01 J=1u TL=0 ...
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt MOTOR_DC P N SPEED params: R=2 L=1m KE=0.01 KT=0.01 J=1u B=1u TL=0
Rm P n1 {R}
Lm n1 n2 {L}
Vi n2 n3 0
Bemf n3 N V = {KE} * V(w)
* Mechanics: node w = speed in rad/s (1 V = 1 rad/s)
Cj w 0 {J}
Rb w 0 {1 / B}
Bt 0 w I = {KT} * I(Vi) - {TL} * tanh(V(w) / 10)
Bspeed SPEED 0 V = V(w) * 60 / (2 * 3.14159265) / 1000
.ends MOTOR_DC

* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* L298N: dual full bridge, pins in the order of the KiCad symbol
* Driver_Motor:L298N (Multiwatt15):
*   1 SENSE_A  2 OUT1  3 OUT2  4 VS  5 IN1  6 ENA  7 IN2  8 GND
*   9 VSS  10 IN3  11 ENB  12 IN4  13 OUT3  14 OUT4  15 SENSE_B
* Inputs: high above 2.3 V (3.3 V and 5 V logic). EN low: outputs released.
* Outputs: high side VS - 1.35 V - 1.0 ohm * I, low side SENSE + 1.2 V
* + 1.0 ohm * I (about 2 V total drop at 0.5 A, as the datasheet);
* free-wheel diodes OUTx -> VS and GND -> OUTx (as on the L298N modules).
* SENSE_A / SENSE_B: tie to GND, or through a sense resistor.
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt L298N SENSE_A OUT1 OUT2 VS IN1 ENA IN2 GND VSS IN3 ENB IN4 OUT3 OUT4 SENSE_B
* Logic levels (smooth threshold at 2.3 V): 1 = high
Bena ena 0 V = 1 / (1 + exp(-(V(ENA,GND) - 2.3) * 40))
Benb enb 0 V = 1 / (1 + exp(-(V(ENB,GND) - 2.3) * 40))
Bin1 in1 0 V = 1 / (1 + exp(-(V(IN1,GND) - 2.3) * 40))
Bin2 in2 0 V = 1 / (1 + exp(-(V(IN2,GND) - 2.3) * 40))
Bin3 in3 0 V = 1 / (1 + exp(-(V(IN3,GND) - 2.3) * 40))
Bin4 in4 0 V = 1 / (1 + exp(-(V(IN4,GND) - 2.3) * 40))
* Half bridges: high side to VS, low side to SENSE
B1h GND OUT1 I = V(ena) * V(in1) * max(V(VS,GND) - 1.35 - V(OUT1,GND), 0) / 1.0
B1l OUT1 SENSE_A I = V(ena) * (1 - V(in1)) * max(V(OUT1,SENSE_A) - 1.2, 0) / 1.0
B2h GND OUT2 I = V(ena) * V(in2) * max(V(VS,GND) - 1.35 - V(OUT2,GND), 0) / 1.0
B2l OUT2 SENSE_A I = V(ena) * (1 - V(in2)) * max(V(OUT2,SENSE_A) - 1.2, 0) / 1.0
B3h GND OUT3 I = V(enb) * V(in3) * max(V(VS,GND) - 1.35 - V(OUT3,GND), 0) / 1.0
B3l OUT3 SENSE_B I = V(enb) * (1 - V(in3)) * max(V(OUT3,SENSE_B) - 1.2, 0) / 1.0
B4h GND OUT4 I = V(enb) * V(in4) * max(V(VS,GND) - 1.35 - V(OUT4,GND), 0) / 1.0
B4l OUT4 SENSE_B I = V(enb) * (1 - V(in4)) * max(V(OUT4,SENSE_B) - 1.2, 0) / 1.0
* Free-wheel diodes
D1h OUT1 VS dfw
D1l GND OUT1 dfw
D2h OUT2 VS dfw
D2l GND OUT2 dfw
D3h OUT3 VS dfw
D3l GND OUT3 dfw
D4h OUT4 VS dfw
D4l GND OUT4 dfw
.model dfw D(IS=1n RS=0.1 N=1.5 CJO=50p TT=50n)
* Leakage of the released outputs, logic inputs (about 100 uA at 5 V)
Ro1 OUT1 GND 100k
Ro2 OUT2 GND 100k
Ro3 OUT3 GND 100k
Ro4 OUT4 GND 100k
Rin1 IN1 GND 50k
Rin2 IN2 GND 50k
Rin3 IN3 GND 50k
Rin4 IN4 GND 50k
Rena ENA GND 50k
Renb ENB GND 50k
* Supplies: logic (about 13 mA on VSS), power stage at rest (about 10 mA on VS)
Rvss VSS GND 390
Rvs VS GND 1.2k
.ends L298N
